routing-switching-design is the vendor-neutral routing and switching DESIGN umbrella: topology
selection, redundancy-model selection, segmentation design, and platform comparison. It is the
design-and-selection counterpart to the vault's existing diagnostic skills (igp-routing-analysis,
bgp-analysis, evpn-vxlan-fabric) and to the diagnose-first operating entry point
(multi-vendor-network-ops). Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Scope boundary (decided with the user at plan time, 2026-06-17): this skill owns DESIGN /
ARCHITECTURE-SELECTION / PLATFORM-COMPARISON only. ALL protocol and fabric TROUBLESHOOTING is routed
out via "When not to use" to the four existing skills, so there is zero diagnostic duplication:
  - OSPF / EIGRP / IS-IS diagnostics      -> igp-routing-analysis (already on disk, Apache-2.0)
  - BGP diagnostics                        -> bgp-analysis (already on disk)
  - EVPN-VXLAN fabric troubleshooting      -> evpn-vxlan-fabric (already on disk, Apache-2.0)
  - diagnose-first multi-vendor operations -> multi-vendor-network-ops (already on disk)
The chrishuffman5 source umbrella mixes design tables with protocol-fundamentals (BGP path selection,
OSPF area/LSA types, EVPN route types). Those protocol fundamentals were deliberately NOT folded here;
they are owned by bgp-analysis / igp-routing-analysis / evpn-vxlan-fabric. Only the design / selection
material was carried over, re-authored vendor-neutral.

